Notes on Recode File

1.     The sample selected for the individual survey was an ever married sample.  To produce estimates for all women it is
       necessary to apply inflation factors to account for the proportion of women never married.  The factors are stored in
       the following variables:

              AWFACTT        All women factor for the total sample.
              AWFACTU        All women factor for urban/rural breakdowns (V102).
              AWFACTR        All women factor for regional breakdowns (V101).
              AWFACTE        All women factor for educational breakdowns (V106).
              AWFACTE5       All women factor for educational breakdowns with 5 values (S110,S111).

       These factors are stored in 5 digit variables, with two implied decimal places.  A value of 00150 means an inflation
       factor of 1.5 should be applied to this individual case to allow for never married women.  This means that for every
       two married women found in the household schedule of a particular age and with the same background characteristic,
       there are 3 women in total, i.e. the two married women plus one never married woman.  These inflation factors have
       been used in the calculation of fertility rates, median ages at first marriage and first birth, mean number of children
       ever born, etc.

2.     Section 97 contains the maternal mortality section, listing the siblings of the respondents and their survival status. 
       Please see the questionnaire for skip instructions.

3.     Only currently married women were asked V312, V313 and V526.  V312 and V313 for women not currently married
       have been assigned a code of zero (0) assuming that they are not current users.  V526 is coded not applicable for those
       women.

4.     For V304 through V309 and V314, the following are codes for country specific other methods: (13) Breastfeeding (14)
       Seeds and (15) Some Pill/Aspirin.

5.     Because the series of questions in the Health section that query a recent fever or cough episode are very different for
       the Core questionnaire, they have not been placed in H22-H38 (REC43).  Rather the complete series can be found
       in REC95, variables S426 through s432H.  Treatment for the most recent diarrheal incident can also be found in
       REC95, variables S435-S444M.

6.     Because age at first intercourse was not asked in the Sudan DHS, V525 has been coded "96", question not asked.


Inconsistencies in the Recode file

1.     There are 37 cases in which the respondent was sexually active in the last 4 weeks, but her responses did not permit
       standard coding in V527 and V528.  These variables have been coded (995) and (95) - within the last 4 weeks, exact
       time not specified.

2.     There are 3 cases in which ever use of female sterilization (V305(6)) is coded as "yes" (1) but current use (V312) is
       coded as zero (0), not using.  These respondents are not currently married and were not asked the question about
       current use.

3.     There are 6 cases in which current use (V312) is coded as "other method" (10) while V305 for method 10 is not
       applicable.  For 4 of these cases, ever use of method 15 (V305(14)) is coded "yes" (1) and for 2 of these cases, ever
       use of method 15 (V305(15)) is coded "yes" (1).

4.     There is 1 case for which M6 - duration of amenorrhea - is longer than the interval between births.

5.     There is 1 case for which M8 - duration of postpartum abstinence - is longer than the interval between births.


